      "math_academy_id": "e-8601",
      "problem": "Given that $X \\sim \\textrm{Bernoulli}(0.65),$ compute $P(X = 0).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X \\sim \\textrm{Bernoulli}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14273447/assets/22daada176376db25cf6a619b2aed090022436837f928cca43697f9473d88822.svg)\n\nHere, $X \\sim \\textrm{Bernoulli}(0.65),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14273447/assets/b434e597afbc6be42222001956380565e27a423910a9ecf61dfd883a3874df90.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X = 0) = f(0) = 0.35.\n$$",
